(*
env: OEVM_NO_DISPLAY=1
expect:
caught displayUnavailable
text no display on this board
refresh also raised
finished
*)
(* tuvm#88 — a board can genuinely lack the panel (the MagTag's own two
   revisions differ in which controller they carry, and most boards have no
   display node at all), so `#displayUnavailable` is a condition a node must be
   able to catch and carry on headless from. That path had NO host coverage:
   `display_target_available()` was hard-coded to 1 on the host, so every host
   test saw a display and the raise was unreachable.

   `OEVM_NO_DISPLAY=1` (platform.c) is the seam that makes it reachable — the
   same shape as `OEVM_GC_STRESS` in gc.c. It is delivered by the `env:` header
   above rather than exported globally, because a global export would make
   01_display_grid and 02_display_raises assert against a display that reports
   itself absent.

   The tag is asserted, not merely the fact that something failed — an untagged
   catch would pass even if the raise came from somewhere else entirely. Same
   discipline as 13_pulse/03_gpio_undeclared_raises.nsl.

   Both a write AND a refresh are exercised: all four seam functions answer nil
   under this condition, and a node that caught only the first would still wedge
   on the second. *)
class DisplayUnavailable packageUsing: manifest = () (
  public main: platform args: args = (
    | display |
    display:: platform display.

    [ display at: 0 col: 0 put: 'HI' ]
      on: [ :e | e tag = #displayUnavailable ]
      do: [ :e | 'caught displayUnavailable' out.
                 ('text ' , (e at: #text ifAbsent: [ '?' ])) out ].

    [ display refresh ]
      on: [ :e | e tag = #displayUnavailable ]
      do: [ :e | 'refresh also raised' out ].

    'finished' out.
  )
) : (
)
